<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong Motor 1996 yr loss rises.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong Motor 1996 yr loss rises.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31</p>
<p>	 (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net (both loss)			  228.5 vs 126.2</p>
<p>    Turnover				 1,369.4 vs 986.7</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		   (loss) 8.5 vs  4.9 (gain)</p>
<p>    Div Register				  Dec 31</p>
<p>NOTE: Ssangyong Motor Co Ltd, a unit of the Ssangyong Group SSYG.CN, said the rise in losses stemmed largely from rising financial costs on loans the company took out to expand production lines. The company's share capital stood at 44.74 million at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5645</p>
